python3-pygame
python3-gpiozero
python3-venv
network-manager
polkitd
python3-cryptography
ca-certificates
python3-paho-mqtt
# iw: since the root went read-only (OTA design 4.3) scoreboard-netcfg sets
# the Wi-Fi regulatory domain with `iw reg set` itself, on every boot, instead
# of through raspi-config, which wrote under /etc and into cmdline.txt. Lite
# images ship iw already; naming it makes that a dependency rather than luck.
iw

# --- The display path (added 2026-09-18, after v0.1.1) ---
#
# SDL's kmsdrm backend dlopens these by soname at runtime rather than linking
# them, so NOTHING in the image depends on them and apt installs none of them
# on its own. Recommends would not have helped either: libsdl2-2.0-0
# (2.32.4+dfsg-1) Depends on libdrm2 and libgbm1 among others, Suggests only
# xdg-utils, and Recommends nothing at all. A desktop image hides the gap
# because its desktop pulls the whole stack in for its own reasons; a Lite
# appliance image does not. v0.1.1 shipped without them and crash-looped on
# "EGL not initialized" (docs/hardware-checks.md, H5).
#
# libegl1          libEGL.so.1, the glvnd dispatcher SDL_egl.c opens by that
#                  exact soname. Pulls libglvnd0 and libegl-mesa0.
# libegl-mesa0     libEGL_mesa.so.0, the Mesa EGL vendor library the
#                  dispatcher loads, plus /usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/
#                  50_mesa.json, the vendor file without which the dispatcher
#                  finds no driver. Named explicitly rather than left to
#                  libegl1's Depends, so the vendor half cannot go missing
#                  silently.
# libgles2         libGLESv2.so.2, which SDL loads before EGL and retries as
#                  GLES 2.0 when its desktop-GL attempt fails.
#
# libgl1 is deliberately absent, but NOT for the reason first written here.
# That reason was "SDL's ES2 retry covers the missing libGL.so.1". Corrected
# 2026-09-19: the retry covers WINDOW CREATION only (KMSDRM_CreateWindow,
# SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c:1552). The window-framebuffer path is separate --
# SDL_CreateWindowTexture (SDL_video.c:230) picks a 2D renderer by walking
# render_drivers[] (SDL_render.c:100), where "opengl" precedes "opengles2",
# and with no libGL.so.1 that attempt fails after destroying and recreating
# the kmsdrm window twice. v0.1.2 showed a black panel for fifteen minutes
# because of it. The fix is in the units (SDL_FRAMEBUFFER_ACCELERATION and
# SDL_RENDER_DRIVER, both = opengles2), not a package. Do NOT add libgl1
# here: spec 9.2 explains why naming the renderer is the smaller change.
#
# The drivers themselves were never missing. libEGL_mesa.so.0 and libgbm1's
# backend gbm/dri_gbm.so both carry DT_NEEDED on libgallium-26.2.2-...so, and
# the vc4 and v3d gallium drivers are compiled into libgallium (its strings
# carry VC4_DEBUG and V3D_DEBUG) -- so mesa-libgallium, which v0.1.1 already
# had through libgbm1, was always enough. Neither library imports dlopen at
# all, and no "%s_dri.so" template exists anywhere on this path.
#
# libgl1-mesa-dri  NOT on the load path, as far as static analysis of the
#                  26.2.2 debs can show: every dri/*_dri.so in it is a symlink
#                  to libdril_dri.so, a shim that dlopens libEGL.so.1 itself
#                  -- Mesa's legacy-DRI-over-EGL layer for the X server, which
#                  sits downstream of this path rather than under it. Kept for
#                  this release anyway: it is ~50 kB, and being wrong about it
#                  costs a 35-minute build plus a person with a card reader,
#                  which is a worse trade than carrying it. REMOVE IT once a
#                  real boot has rendered without it (docs/hardware-checks.md,
#                  H1) -- tracked there as a follow-up, not left to rot here.
#
# libgbm1, mesa-libgallium and libdrm2 are not repeated here: libgbm1 and
# libdrm2 are libsdl2-2.0-0's own Depends, and mesa-libgallium arrives through
# libgbm1. tools/image-gate.sh asserts the six files that actually carry the
# display, by path, so a future apt change cannot quietly drop one.
libegl1
libegl-mesa0
libgles2
libgl1-mesa-dri
